{"id": "2026-07-30-news-us-strikes-iran-irgc-vows-retaliation", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "US strikes Iran, IRGC vows retaliation", "summary": "US CENTCOM struck dozens of IRGC targets across Iran overnight into 30 July, killing three civilians in Qeshm; Iran fired missiles at Jordan and Kuwait and vowed retaliation.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/30/us-hits-multiple-targets-in-iran-as-irgc-pledges-retaliation-what-we-know", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "US Central Command struck dozens of Iranian military targets overnight into Thursday 30 July, killing at least three civilians in Qeshm, and Iran vowed swift retaliation. CENTCOM (US Central Command — the American military command covering the Middle East) said it hit dozens of IRGC (Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps — Iran's elite armed branch) sites, including command centres, missile and drone facilities and coastal-surveillance and maritime assets, calling it a \"powerful response\" to an Iranian ballistic-missile attack on a US base in Jordan a day earlier. Iranian state media (IRIB, Tasnim, Fars) reported explosions across the south — on Qeshm and Kish islands, in Bushehr province (home to Iran's only nuclear power plant), and in Ahvaz and Bandar Abbas; in Qeshm city a strike on a residential building killed a couple and their two-year-old child, with rescuers still digging for others trapped. The IRGC said \"the aggressor will be punished\"; Jordan's army said it intercepted five Iranian missiles on Thursday morning, and Kuwait reported one worker killed when a building belonging to a Chinese company was hit.", "why": "US and Iranian forces have traded blows repeatedly since a June ceasefire brokered at Switzerland's Bürgenstock collapsed, and the confrontation is spreading — to Kuwait and Jordan, to Red Sea shipping, and to Egypt, where a drone struck two ships at the port of Damietta on Wednesday.", "thread_id": "2026-06-20-cyber-papers-iran-closes-strait-of-hormuz-again-over-israeli", "first_seen_date": "2026-06-20", "event_date": "2026-07-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Iran", "United States", "IRGC", "Qeshm", "Jordan"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-japan-quake-toll-climbs-past-30", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "Japan quake toll climbs past 30", "summary": "The death toll from Tuesday's magnitude-6.8 Kumamoto earthquake rose to about 30 as rescuers searched a shopping centre and paper mill.", "url": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/jul/30/japan-earthquake-death-toll-rises", "source_domain": "theguardian.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing", "disputed"], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The death toll from the earthquake that hit south-western Japan on Tuesday 28 July rose to about 30 on Thursday, as rescuers battled heat and aftershocks. The magnitude-6.8 quake — which some earlier reports put at 7.1 — struck Kumamoto prefecture on the island of Kyushu, injured at least 62 people and registered the maximum level 7 on Japan's shindo scale (a measure of ground-shaking intensity, distinct from magnitude). Nearly 5,000 Self-Defence Force troops worked in temperatures up to 35°C after a magnitude-5.8 aftershock overnight; teams were still searching an Aeon shopping centre in Kashima, where a gas explosion after evacuation killed six shop workers who had gone back inside, and a Nippon Paper mill in Yatsushiro, where a collapsed chimney killed eight. Some 75,000 homes lost running water and 23,000 lost power. Toyota, Honda, Sony and Renesas paused some production in Kyushu — a hub for about a fifth of the region's auto and semiconductor output — while TSMC resumed operations; analysts said the halts looked precautionary rather than damage-driven.", "why": "Kyushu's chip and car plants sit in a global supply chain, so even precautionary shutdowns ripple outward; the 2016 Kumamoto quakes killed 273.", "thread_id": "2026-07-28-news-m7-1-quake-strikes-southern-japan", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-28", "event_date": "2026-07-28", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Japan", "Kumamoto", "Kyushu"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-russia-s-overnight-barrage-kills-eight-in-ukrain", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "Russia's overnight barrage kills eight in Ukraine", "summary": "Russia fired about 70 missiles and 280 drones at Ukraine overnight into 30 July, killing at least eight including two girls in Kryvyi Rih.", "url": "https://www.dw.com/en/deaths-in-ukraine-after-zelenskyy-warns-of-russian-strikes/a-78167375", "source_domain": "dw.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["ongoing"], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Russia fired roughly 70 missiles and 280 drones at Ukraine overnight into Thursday 30 July, killing at least eight people, hours after President Volodymyr Zelensky had warned of an imminent \"massive\" strike. At least six of the dead, including two girls, were killed in a missile strike on the central city of Kryvyi Rih; one person died in Kyiv and fatalities were reported as far west as Lviv, with Zelensky saying more than 10 regions were hit. Ukraine remains critically short of Patriot interceptors — the only munitions able to down Russia's ballistic missiles — a shortage that has worsened since the US–Israel war on Iran drew down Western air-defence stocks; Zelensky said US President Donald Trump has now authorised Ukraine to build Patriot interceptors on its own soil.", "why": "The barrage extends an intensifying Russian air campaign that has repeatedly struck Kyiv and other cities through July, even as Ukraine's ability to intercept the incoming missiles thins.", "thread_id": "2026-05-20-cyber-papers-russia-ukraine-largest-aerial-campaign-of-the-wa", "first_seen_date": "2026-05-20", "event_date": "2026-07-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Ukraine", "Russia", "Kryvyi Rih", "Patriot"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-rushdie-s-attacker-convicted-of-terrorism", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "Rushdie's attacker convicted of terrorism", "summary": "A US court convicted Hadi Matar of terrorism charges over the 2022 stabbing of author Salman Rushdie; he is already serving 25 years.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/30/man-who-stabbed-author-salman-rushdie-convicted-of-terrorism-charges", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A US court convicted Hadi Matar of terrorism charges on Thursday 30 July over the 2022 stabbing of author Salman Rushdie. The jury found Matar — who is already serving a 25-year sentence for attempted murder and assault after the near-fatal attack at a literary event in New York state, which left Rushdie blind in one eye — guilty on the additional counts.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-07-30-news-rushdie-s-attacker-convicted-of-terrorism", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-30", "event_date": "2026-07-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Salman Rushdie", "Hadi Matar", "United States"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-swiss-army-curbs-chinese-connected-cars", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "Swiss army curbs Chinese connected cars", "summary": "Switzerland's DDPS extended counter-espionage rules to restrict connected cars near sensitive military sites after the SRC warned about Chinese vehicles.", "url": "https://www.rts.ch/info/suisse/2026/article/espionnage-le-ddps-limite-l-acces-des-voitures-connectees-29315725.html", "source_domain": "rts.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Switzerland's defence department (DDPS) has extended its counter-espionage rules to keep connected cars away from sensitive military sites, RTS reported on 29 July. The restrictions apply near installations such as the army's electronic-warfare centre at Zimmerwald (Bern), though the DDPS would not detail them. They follow the first-ever warning by the Federal Intelligence Service (SRC), in its annual security report, about connected vehicles — especially Chinese ones; SRC director Serge Bavaud said on 25 June that people likely to interest foreign spies should avoid Chinese connected cars, calling them \"smartphones on wheels\" whose cameras and microphones could hand recorded conversations to Chinese intelligence. Carmaker BYD says it strictly complies with EU and Swiss data-protection rules and transmits no data to China.", "why": "Switzerland joins Germany — where Bavaria has opened an inquiry — and the US, which banned imports of Chinese and Russian connected vehicles in 2025, in treating cheap, data-rich cars as a surveillance risk.", "thread_id": "2026-07-30-news-swiss-army-curbs-chinese-connected-cars", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-30", "event_date": "2026-07-29", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["DDPS", "SRC", "BYD", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-kof-barometer-rises-again-in-july", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "KOF barometer rises again in July", "summary": "The KOF Economic Barometer rose 1.4 points to 103.5 in July, ETH Zurich said, signalling improving Swiss growth prospects led by industry and services.", "url": "https://kof.ethz.ch/en/news-and-events/media/press-releases/2026/07/kof_economic_barometer_outlook_improves_again.html", "source_domain": "kof.ethz.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["official PR"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The KOF Economic Barometer rose 1.4 points to 103.5 in July, the ETH Zurich institute reported on Thursday 30 July, pointing to improving near-term prospects for the Swiss economy. The barometer is a leading composite indicator of where Swiss GDP is heading; readings above roughly 100 signal above-average growth, and July's is its strongest since a slump in March after the Middle East war shock (June was revised to 102.1). The institute said the gains were broad across the production side — financial and insurance services, other services, construction and manufacturing all improved.", "why": "After months below its medium-term average, the index now sits comfortably above it for a second month, a modestly reassuring signal for jobs and investment in an economy exposed to global shocks.", "thread_id": "2026-07-30-news-kof-barometer-rises-again-in-july", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-30", "event_date": "2026-07-30", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["KOF", "ETH Zurich", "Switzerland"]}
{"id": "2026-07-30-news-92-000-romands-hunt-homes-in-france", "date": "2026-07-30", "stream": "news", "headline": "92,000 Romands hunt homes in France", "summary": "Over 92,000 French-speaking Swiss are actively seeking housing across the border in France to escape high Swiss costs, a Comparis study found.", "url": "https://www.rts.ch/info/suisse/2026/article/plus-de-92-000-romands-cherchent-un-logement-en-france-voisine-29316082.html", "source_domain": "rts.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "More than 92,000 French-speaking Swiss are actively looking for housing across the border in neighbouring France to escape high domestic costs, according to a Comparis study reported on 30 July. Seven in ten of those surveyed cited high rents and purchase prices, with Geneva residents the most drawn to France; a quarter of Romand households already spend at least 36% of their budget on housing, above the usual roughly one-third guideline. Four in ten said family distance and longer commutes hold them back from actually moving.", "why": "The numbers put a figure on a pressure the reader lives with — Swiss housing costs pushing residents to weigh a cross-border move — even as border towns absorb the demand.", "thread_id": "2026-07-30-news-92-000-romands-hunt-homes-in-france", "first_seen_date": "2026-07-30", "event_date": null, "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Comparis", "Switzerland", "France", "Geneva"]}
